Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:26:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1027/1179] Settings kept on disk, a reset, and a memory preset
 that stays as chosen

- heresy-settings.js mirrors the page settings (its yue2.* keys) to the lab, which keeps them
  in the user config folder: ~/.config/yue2_os/settings.json (%APPDATA% on Windows,
  Application Support on a Mac). Read synchronously before app.js; keys the browser lacks
  come from the file, the newer side wins where both hold one, a browser meeting the file
  for the first time keeps its own. Writes are merges of changed and deliberately removed
  keys; a mass disappearance (site data cleared under a live page) sends no removals, and
  nothing is written when the file could not be read at load. The OpenRouter key and the
  jobs list stay in the browser.
- Engine room: "Page settings" in the Server card, and a Reset page settings button.
- GPU memory preset: the server keeps the knobs, not the name, and 24 and 32 GB differ by
  Keep models loaded alone, so ticking it made F5 show 32. The choice is remembered and shown
  while its model, context and VAE tiles hold; keep-loaded is a choice within a preset. Sizes
  above the GPU found are marked, and Auto names what it found.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
